{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "המצוה הזאת לפני ה' אלהינו", :translit "ha-mitzvah ha-zot lifnei Hashem Elokeinu", :gloss "this commandment before YHWH our God"} {:he "לפני", :translit "lifnei", :gloss "before"} {:he "לפני ולפנים", :translit "lifnei ulifnim", :gloss "before and within"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Word repetition: לפני appears twice in the verse, signaling entry into the innermost sanctuary."}], :frame {:text "The phrase לפני ולפנים denotes the innermost sanctum, the space beyond the Hall, as described in the layout of the Temple in Mishnah Middot 4:7 and used in Mishnah Yoma 5:1 for the High Priest's entry on Yom Kippur.", :sources ["Mishnah Middot 4:7" "Mishnah Yoma 5:1"]}} {:quotes [{:he "כאשר צונו", :translit "ka'asher tzivvanu", :gloss "as He commanded us"} {:he "כי יביאך", :translit "ki yevi'akha", :gloss "that He will bring you"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Linkage: the words כאשר צונו in our verse connect to the phrase כי יביאך, and through the merit of the commandments Israel merits being brought into the land."}], :frame {:text "The principle that reward comes בשכר המצות, in the merit of the commandments, is a foundational rabbinic concept found in sources such as Devarim Rabbah 1:18 and reflected in the teaching of Shimon HaTzaddik in Avot 1:3 that the world stands on three things including the service of commandments.", :sources ["Devarim Rabbah 1:18" "Mishnah Avot 1:3"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Word repetition: לפני appears twice in the verse, signaling entry into the innermost sanctuary.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Linkage: the words כאשר צונו in our verse connect to the phrase כי יביאך, and through the merit of the commandments Israel merits being brought into the land.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:34:56.092080699Z", :model "glm-5.2"}